  "verdict": "If active_set_transitions is empty across the sweep, the active set is q-CONSTANT \u2014 metallic structure does not reach the LP combinatorial output at n=2.  If transitions exist AT metallic ratios, sharpened (M2) is confirmed at this level.  If transitions exist elsewhere, the LP-vertex structure is driven by character zeros (same pattern as the Jones / n=4 probes), not by metallic ratios.",
  "limitations": [
    "n=2 has only 2 LP variables and 2 Frobenius constraints \u2014 the smallest non-trivial case.  Higher-n LPs (n=3 Borromean d=6) have richer active-set structure but require explicit Markov-trace + Gram tabulation.",
    "Mahler-height proxy uses `Fraction.limit_denominator(10^6)`. At metallic q the value (q - q\u207b\u00b9) IS an integer to machine precision so the proxy hits 0 floor; at generic q the proxy grows with denominator complexity.  Not a true Mahler measure, but tracks the right structural distinction.",
    "scipy.linprog uses HIGHS solver in double precision; for a true algebraic-integer LP at q = \u03b4_n we'd need a symbolic solver (sympy or QSOpt-Ex).  This probe shows the floating-point shadow."
  ]
